        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(minimax): apply request policy to media generation requests",
        "body": "## Summary\n- MiniMax video, music, and image generation now pass `models.providers.<providerId>.request` into provider HTTP resolution instead of silently ignoring configured request overrides.\n- Removes the image caller-level hard-coded `allowPrivateNetwork: false` so configured request policy can control private-network access while the default remains deny-by-default when no request override is configured.\n- collision check: searched `minimax request policy`, `minimax allowPrivateNetwork`, and `minimax video proxy`; no same-file or same-problem open PR was found for these MiniMax media generation paths.\n\n## Verification\n- `TMPDIR=/media/vdc/0668001470/tmp/openclaw-task-tmp node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/minimax/video-generation-provider.test.ts extensions/minimax/music-generation-provider.test.ts extensions/minimax/image-generation-provider.test.ts` - passed; `Test Files  3 passed (3)`, `Tests  29 passed (29)`.\n- `TMPDIR=/media/vdc/0668001470/tmp/openclaw-task-tmp OPENCLAW_OXLINT_SKIP_PREPARE=1 node scripts/run-oxlint.mjs --tsconfig config/tsconfig/oxlint.extensions.json extensions/minimax/video-generation-provider.ts extensions/minimax/video-generation-provider.test.ts extensions/minimax/music-generation-provider.ts extensions/minimax/music-generation-provider.test.ts extensions/minimax/image-generation-provider.ts extensions/minimax/image-generation-provider.test.ts extensions/minimax/provider-http.test-helpers.ts` - passed; exit 0.\n- `git diff --check` - passed; exit 0.\n- mutation check: temporarily removing the image `request:` parameter made `extensions/minimax/image-generation-provider.test.ts` fail because `resolveProviderHttpRequestConfig` no longer received the configured request object; restoring the patch returned the test to green.\n- mutation check from the original commit: temporarily removing the video and music `request:` parameters made the focused Vitest fail with `expected undefined to deeply equal { allowPrivateNetwork: true, headers: ... }` in both portal media tests; restoring the patch returned the test to green.\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\nBehavior addressed: MiniMax video/music/image generation now honor configured provider request overrides such as custom headers and `allowPrivateNetwork` for the active provider id. The actual network-path proof below exercises video and music against a local MiniMax-compatible `node:http` endpoint; image is covered by a focused regression because MiniMax image generation intentionally uses a dedicated fixed regional endpoint rather than the text/media `baseUrl`.\n\nReal environment tested: local Linux Node source checkout; actual exported MiniMax portal video and music provider builders; local `node:http` server; no third-party MiniMax network traffic; proxy env vars unset for the proof process.\n\nExact command run after this patch:\n\n```text\nenv HTTP_PROXY= HTTPS_PROXY= http_proxy= https_proxy= ALL_PROXY= all_proxy= NO_PROXY= no_proxy= node --import tsx scratchpad/minimax-request-policy-proof.mts\n```\n\nThe temporary proof script was not committed. It configured `models.providers.minimax-portal.request` with `allowPrivateNetwork: true` and `headers: { \"X-MiniMax-Proof\": \"policy-applied\" }`, then called the real MiniMax portal video and music providers against the local endpoint.\n\nObserved output after fix:\n\n```text\nminimax-request-policy-proof\nvideo_files=1\nmusic_files=1\nprovider_paths=/v1/video_generation,/v1/query/video_generation?task_id=video-task,/v1/music_generation\nproof_headers=policy-applied,policy-applied,policy-applied\nauth_headers=Bearer ***,Bearer ***,Bearer ***\n```\n\nEvidence after fix: the local endpoint received configured request headers on the actual video submit request, video poll request, and music generation request, and both providers returned generated media. The image regression separately verifies the image provider passes the same sanitized request object to provider HTTP resolution and that the final image POST receives `allowPrivateNetwork: true` plus the configured header.\n",
        "branch": "alix/minimax-media-request-policy",
